# XBD 9.2 Regular Expression General Requirements
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Newline as an ordinary character in the functions, REG_ICASE and the
# 256-byte minimum for plain literals are tested by XSH.regcomp.029,
# XSH.regcomp.027 and XSH.regcomp.036; this module adds the 256-byte limit
# for other constructs.

assertion  XBD.9.2-general.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap09.html#9.2
class      required
since      1992
says       REs of exactly 256 bytes built from other constructs are accepted and
           work, in a BRE and an ERE: a bracket expression of 254 list characters, 84
           alternatives followed by a literal run, groups nested 63 (BRE) and 127
           (ERE) deep, 28 (BRE) and 36 (ERE) interval expressions, 128 escaped periods and 128 starred
           items.
test       t/001-limit-shapes.c
